The [full paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.09638) provides reverse-mathematical results for infinite hypergraphs, not distributional hardness for planted finite colorings.

Key findings:

- Finite planted coloring passes G and V.
- Track A fails: no theorem supports hardness of the generated distribution.
- Track B fails: BFS color propagation and the shortest compact route are identical—16,895 operations versus 16,895 at the 256-atom limit.
- The genuinely infinite results lack bounded, executable witnesses.
- Finite Matryoshka instances are explicitly solved in the paper by coloring the largest vertex differently.

Per the instructions, no generator or hardening artifacts were created after the STEP 0 rejection.
